{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0210"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge history/early-modern","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/history__early-modern.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",630],["+","1605 | Gunpowder Plot in London | Catholic anger at James I |\n| "],["=",174],["+","In England, Henry's settlement bred its own Catholic backlash. Shortly after midnight on 5 November 1605 Guy Fawkes was arrested in a cellar beneath the House of Lords, guarding 36 barrels of gunpowder: Robert Catesby's conspirators, disappointed that King James I had not eased the laws against Catholics, had planned to blow up Parliament (the House of Lords) at the State Opening and kill the king with it. The Gunpowder Plot is still remembered every 5 November with bonfires and fireworks on Guy Fawkes Night.\n\n"],["=",2],["-","century"],["+","few"],["=",1],["+","years "],["=",363]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",606],["+","1605 | Pulververschwörung in London | Katholischer Zorn auf Jakob I. |\n| "],["=",166],["-","Ein"],["+","In"],["=",1],["-","Jahrhundert"],["+","England"],["=",1],["+","brachte Heinrichs Kirchenordnung ihren eigenen katholischen Gegenschlag hervor. Kurz nach Mitternacht am 5. November 1605 wurde Guy Fawkes in einem Keller unter dem House of Lords verhaftet, wo er 36 Fässer Schießpulver bewachte: Robert Catesbys Verschwörer, enttäuscht, dass König Jakob I. die Gesetze gegen Katholiken nicht gelockert hatte, wollten bei der feierlichen Parlamentseröffnung das Parlament (House of Lords) in die Luft sprengen und den König mit ihm töten. An die Pulververschwörung erinnern bis heute jeden 5. November Freudenfeuer und Feuerwerke zur Guy Fawkes Night.\n\nWenige Jahre "],["=",337]]}]},
